Contributions

The contribution workflow described in CONTRIBUTING.md — fork the repository,
create a task branch, modify the code there and open a pull request against
`dev` — is expressly permitted by this licence and needs no separate written
permission. That permission covers the fork, the local modifications and the
pull request itself, and it ends when the pull request is closed without being
merged.

By opening a pull request you agree that your contribution is provided under
the terms of this licence and that the copyright holder may use, modify,
distribute and sublicense it as part of this software. Any use that goes beyond
the contribution workflow above still requires the prior written permission of
the copyright holder.

